    <string name="th_info">What does this do?</string>
    <string name="info_from">The language the comic is written in. The text on the page is read (OCR) in this language. Inside the reader the app also picks it from the source when the source tells its language.</string>
    <string name="info_to">The language you want to read in. Every translation, the glossary and the collection are kept per language.</string>
    <string name="info_auto">When a chapter finishes downloading it is translated in the background at once, so it opens already translated. Uses your keys for every downloaded chapter.</string>
    <string name="info_team">Your AI keys. All translation is done by AI: with one key it works alone, with more keys a chapter is split between them by each key\'s strength and every page\'s weight, so it finishes faster. A key that is busy or out of quota rests and its work goes to the others. Each key is checked by itself: speed, model and how much is left today.</string>
    <string name="info_mode">Fast: the team translates, the collection and the automatic checks fix what they can. Accurate: the same, then the strongest key reviews the whole chapter and fixes mistakes (one more request per chapter, better quality).</string>
    <string name="info_vision">Keys that can read images also get the page pictures, so they see who is speaking and the text the OCR missed. Better translation, a bit more quota.</string>
    <string name="info_instructions">Your own instructions for the translator: tone, how to write names, words to keep, the dialect of the dialogue. They go with every request.</string>
    <string name="info_temperature">How free the AI is with wording. Lower (0.2) is more literal and steady, higher (0.8) is more creative. 0.4 suits most comics.</string>
    <string name="info_max_output">The longest answer the AI may write in one request. Raise it only when long chapters come back cut short.</string>
    <string name="info_no_key_engine">Used only when there is no working AI key: ML Kit translates on the phone without internet, Google Translate online. As soon as you add a key, the AI team takes over.</string>
    <string name="info_live">Chapters with no saved translation are translated page by page while you read, starting with the page on screen.</string>
    <string name="info_quick_draft">Inside the reader a quick Google translation shows within a second, and the team\'s translation replaces it when it is ready. Turn it off to see only the AI translation.</string>
    <string name="info_reader_button">The floating translation button inside the chapter. Off: a clean reading screen; translation still works.</string>
    <string name="info_font">The font translated text is drawn with in the bubbles.</string>
    <string name="info_pretranslate">When you pass the middle of a chapter, the next one is downloaded and translated in the background, so it opens translated.</string>
    <string name="info_collection">Every line the team translates is kept on the phone and reused at once in every manhwa: repeated lines cost no request and stay consistent. You can search it, correct lines and set its size.</string>
    <string name="info_lessons">Your corrections and the editor\'s become lessons; every few lessons they are turned into short rules the team follows in the next chapters.</string>
    <string name="info_backup">Saves the glossary, story so far and lessons of your manhwa to one file, to move them to another phone or keep a copy.</string>
